# v1 baked a live Google cookie jar into every image layer via `COPY data/`.
# `data/` is excluded here wholesale; the lexicon is copied explicitly and
# cookies are mounted at runtime, never built in.
data/
# Re-admitted by name so the Dockerfile can COPY them: the NGSL lexicon and the
# channel whitelist are inputs, not secrets. Anything else under data/ —
# cookies above all — stays out of the build context entirely.
!data/ngsl.csv
!data/channels.yml

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
# Both forms are required: a leading-directory-less pattern matches only the
# root. Letting a stale tsbuildinfo through is silent and lethal — `tsc -b`
# trusts it, skips emit, and the image ships with no dist/ at all.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

.git
.gitignore
.github
*.log
coverage
.claude
README.md
